Found by the hub in the amdlab live test with image 01c9716 (2026-11-07). 1) ocp node add synapse --role worker --provider ssh-default --host 10.230.30.50 --gpu without the switch: the Cilium leftover refusal comes, exit 1, nothing installed, but an OCPNode synapse stays with phase Failed. 2) The same command with --clean_cilium_residue: exit 1 after 8 s with exactly the same message, no Pending, no Installing. reconcile_until_ready reads the existing Failed CR and returns its old message; the switch never reaches an install. 3) Only ocp node rm synapse --keep_machine, then node add with --clean_cilium_residue worked: leftovers cleared without a reboot, Ready after 3 min, exit 0. So the advice in share/Rexfile _cilium_residue_switch_text (around line 930: run ocp apply with it again, or ocp node add for a node joined without robocop) leads nowhere for node add. Hub decision (perl-developer-bb), not a maintainer decision: the text says what really works. For a node ocp node add joined without robocop that is first ocp node rm NAME --keep_machine, then ocp node add with --clean_cilium_residue. Failed stays terminal. Also check the ocp apply --clean_cilium_residue path: if a refusal there leaves a Failed OCPNode that blocks the second run the same way, the text must be right for that way too. The test quotes the new wording (t/406-cilium-residue-clean.t pins the old sentence); t/190 and t/219 follow if they check the OCP sentence. Red proof on 01c9716. Order: after k444, fourth card of the round.

Worked by ocp-worker in two rounds and reviewed by ocp-release-1106; POD by ocp-doc-writer.

Apply path, checked as asked:
- Only the first control plane is installed again by the next `ocp apply --clean_cilium_residue`. Its refusal comes during bootstrap, before kubeconfig.yaml or any OCPNode exists.
- police2+ and apply's workers are refused with a Failed OCPNode that no later `ocp apply` drives. The reconcile path joins no control plane, and `missing_worker_ocpnodes` skips an OCPNode that exists.
- `ocp node add` behaves the same: `ensure` keeps Failed, and `reconcile_until_ready` returns 0.

So `share/Rexfile` `_cilium_residue_switch_text` now has two sentences, told apart by `server`:
- First control plane: "run ocp apply with it again."
- A joining node: read PROVIDER and IP in `ocp node ls`, then `ocp node rm NAME --keep_machine`, then `ocp node add NAME [--role control-plane] --provider PROVIDER` with the switch. Add `--host IP` for an ssh provider and any `--node_ip`, `--label`, `--taint` or `--gpu` the node had. After a reboot the add works without the switch. The robocop sentence is kept.

Review round 2 added two things:
- the role, because node add defaults to worker; `_install_server` passes control-plane;
- provider and host, because node add refuses without `--provider` when there are several providers, and without `--host` on ssh.

My choice beyond the hub brief: the Apply.pm `=opt clean_cilium_residue` and Node::Add CILIUM LEFTOVERS POD are corrected too, because they gave the same dead-end advice.

